  "notes": "{干|ほ}す means to dry something by exposing it to air or sun.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {乾|かわ}く (intransitive, to dry)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {洗濯物|せんたくもの}を{干|ほ}す: to hang laundry to dry\n- {布団|ふとん}を{干|ほ}す: to air out a futon\n- {干|ほ}し{物|もの}: things hung out to dry\n- {干|ほ}し{竿|ざお}: drying pole\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {干物|ひもの}: dried fish\n- {干|ほ}しぶどう: raisins (dried grapes)\n- {梅干|うめぼ}し: pickled plum\n\nThe kanji {干|ほ}す relates to drying/draining.",
